# Amendment #58 — workspace-sync Bundle β.1 ergonomics: workspace canonical-source config + pos-sync no-args

2026-04-27. Follow-on to amendment #57 (workspace-sync resolver
cost overhaul, sealed at `e619b6a`). Bundle β splits into three
separate amendments per D-β.4 LOCKED; β.1 is the first
(smallest surface, biggest UX win). β.2 (`pos-new-workspace`)
and β.3 (global install path) follow as same-tree-serialize
amendments.

β.1 closes the "every `pos-sync` invocation requires
`--canonical <path>`" friction. Post-β.1, an operator inside a
workspace runs `pos-sync` with no arguments; the CLI loads
`<workspace>/.pos/sync-config.yaml`'s `canonical_source:` field
(URL or absolute local path) and proceeds with the existing
#56 + #57 sync flow.

Three locked outcome-shape decisions (D-β.1, D-β.2, D-β.4) +
the HALT-FOUND #2 docstring promise drive the surface:

  - **D-β.1 LOCKED** — both URL and absolute-local-path forms
    accepted. URL form clones to `~/.pos/canonical-cache/<repo-id>/`
    (workspace-shared cache). Always-fetch on every invocation
    (`git fetch --all --tags`, ~50ms warm). Anything else
    (relative paths, `file://`, `ssh://`) halts at the URL
    discriminator with a structured error naming the three
    accepted shapes.

  - **D-β.2 LOCKED** — β.1 does NOT introduce
    `pos-new-workspace`; that's β.2's deliverable. β.1 stays
    purely additive to the existing `pos-sync` CLI surface.

  - **D-β.4 LOCKED** — three separate amendments rather than
    one bundle. β.1 ships the schema + loader + CLI integration;
    β.2 composes on β.1's config-file shape; β.3 is independent
    but lands last so it doesn't block β.1 + β.2.

  - **HALT-FOUND #2** — `_resolver_client.py:292`'s docstring
    promised `"workspace-tunable via ~/.pos/sync-config.yaml"`
    but no source ever loaded the file. β.1 lands the schema
    + loader for both `<workspace>/.pos/sync-config.yaml`
    (workspace-local) AND `~/.pos/sync-config.yaml` (user-rooted),
    wires the precedence chain through `cli.py`, and tightens
    the docstring to match the now-wired reality.

Surface added under `workspace-sync/`:

  - `src/workspace_sync/sync_config.py` (NEW, ~120 LOC) —
    `SyncConfig` Pydantic model (`extra="forbid"` per #56
    pattern) with three optional fields: `canonical_source`
    (NEW for β.1), `cumulative_token_budget` and
    `per_conflict_token_budget` (HALT-FOUND #2 closure).
    `load_sync_config(workspace_root) -> SyncConfig` walks the
    precedence chain (workspace-local > ~/-rooted > defaults)
    and merges field-by-field. `canonical_source_kind(source)`
    is the URL-vs-local-path discriminator: starts with
    `http(s)://` or `git@` → "url"; absolute POSIX path →
    "local"; anything else → `ValueError` (D-β.1 LOCKED
    narrowing).

  - `src/workspace_sync/canonical_cache.py` (NEW, ~90 LOC) —
    `derive_repo_id(url)` produces a `host/owner/repo` slug
    (handles https/http/git@ forms; strips `.git` suffix).
    `ensure_cache_clone(url, ref) -> Path` clones to
    `~/.pos/canonical-cache/<repo-id>/` if absent + always
    runs `git fetch --all --tags` per D-β.1 LOCKED.

  - `src/workspace_sync/cli.py` (EXTENDED, +25 / -5 LOC) —
